Ensure root-origin short-code paths are treated as self-links, including canonical host variants. Reject fractional and string expiresInDays values while preserving the existing validation response flow.","decisions":[{"title":"Use a JsonNode creator for expiresInDays","rationale":"Jackson otherwise coerces fractional and textual values into Integer. Parsing the raw JSON node allows only integral numeric values while retaining the existing Integer API and bean validation.","alternatives":["Configure global Jackson coercion rules, which would affect unrelated request models","Change the public request field type, which would break existing callers"]},{"title":"Handle empty public-origin paths explicitly","rationale":"A root public origin has no base path, so generated short-code paths must be matched directly rather than through a prefix expression that requires a double slash.","alternatives":["Add a synthetic slash to the base path, which obscures root-path semantics","Change public-origin normalization, which could affect configured path prefixes"]}]}

